# Review bot configuration sample
#
# Copy to .ai-harness/review-bots.conf in generated projects and adjust the
# enabled reviewers for the local team.
#
# Format:
#   bot-name|cli-command|glab-config-dir|model-flag|default-model|reviewer-env
#
# reviewer-env (optional sixth field) names variables, comma-separated, that this
# reviewer may receive from the caller. The reviewer otherwise starts from an
# empty environment plus a fixed allowlist (PATH, HOME, USER, LOGNAME, TMPDIR,
# TERM, locale), with glab and XDG locations in an empty scratch dir (#457).
# Name an API key the CLI authenticates with, or XDG_DATA_HOME,XDG_CONFIG_HOME for a CLI that
# keeps its login there (opencode). An unset name falls back to the CLI default.
# GLAB_*, GITLAB_*, OAUTH_TOKEN and CI_JOB_TOKEN are refused.
#
# default-model is required for a command with --ignore-user-config (the hard
# boundary against codex's approvals_reviewer auto-approval, #452): the flag
# drops the user's model too, and bot-review.sh refuses to run without one.
# A codex line without the exact flag --ignore-user-config is refused (#521):
# keep it when you copy this file, and fix older copies the same way. Any
# word named codex counts as running codex, so another CLI that takes codex
# or env as a value writes it attached (--agent=codex, not --agent codex),
# and a path given as a word of its own must not end in codex or env.
#
# The reviewer argument to bot-review accepts a comma-separated list (e.g.
# `codex,opencode`) to run multiple reviewers, each posting its own attributed
# note. A diverse pair (different model families) is recommended: models rarely
# flag the same line, so two reviewers catch more real bugs than one.

codex|codex exec --ignore-user-config --sandbox read-only -c model_reasoning_effort=high|~/.config/glab-codex|-m|gpt-5.6-sol
claude|claude -p --output-format text --permission-mode plan --no-session-persistence|~/.config/glab-claude|--model
# opencode|opencode run --agent juststart-review|~/.config/glab-opencode|-m||XDG_DATA_HOME,XDG_CONFIG_HOME
# gemini|agy --mode plan|~/.config/glab-gemini|--model
# pi|pi --tools read,grep,find,ls -p|~/.config/glab-pi|--model
